What does the following snippet print when comparing a copy-constructed object with its source?

```java
class ColorRGB {
    int r, g, b;
    ColorRGB(int r, int g, int b) {
        this.r = r; this.g = g; this.b = b;
    }
    ColorRGB(ColorRGB other) {
        this.r = other.r;
        this.g = other.g;
        this.b = other.b;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ColorRGB c1 = new ColorRGB(255, 0, 128);
        ColorRGB c2 = new ColorRGB(c1);
        System.out.println((c1 == c2) + " " + (c1.r == c2.r));
    }
}
```

