Trace the deep copy implementation in this class. What does it print?

```java
class PayloadNode {
    int count = 5;
    PayloadNode(int c) { this.count = c; }
    PayloadNode(PayloadNode other) { this.count = other.count; }
}
class WrapperUnit {
    PayloadNode node;
    WrapperUnit(PayloadNode n) { this.node = n; }
    WrapperUnit(WrapperUnit other) {
        this.node = new PayloadNode(other.node);
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        WrapperUnit w1 = new WrapperUnit(new PayloadNode(20));
        WrapperUnit w2 = new WrapperUnit(w1);
        w2.node.count = 99;
        System.out.println(w1.node.count + " " + (w1.node == w2.node));
    }
}
```

What does the following snippet print when defensive copying is applied to an array in a copy constructor?

```java
class ArrayKeeper {
    int[] data;
    ArrayKeeper(int[] d) { this.data = d; }
    ArrayKeeper(ArrayKeeper other) {
        this.data = new int[other.data.length];
        System.arraycopy(other.data, 0, this.data, 0, other.data.length);
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] original = {1, 2, 3};
        ArrayKeeper k1 = new ArrayKeeper(original);
        ArrayKeeper k2 = new ArrayKeeper(k1);
        k2.data[0] = 50;
        System.out.println(k1.data[0] + " " + (k1.data == k2.data));
    }
}
```

