Analyze constructor delegation and inheritance in this copy constructor hierarchy. What is output?

```java
class BaseAsset {
    String code;
    BaseAsset(String c) { this.code = c; }
    BaseAsset(BaseAsset other) { this.code = other.code; }
}
class SecuredAsset extends BaseAsset {
    int riskScore;
    SecuredAsset(String c, int r) {
        super(c);
        this.riskScore = r;
    }
    SecuredAsset(SecuredAsset other) {
        super(other);
        this.riskScore = other.riskScore;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SecuredAsset a1 = new SecuredAsset("BOND", 7);
        SecuredAsset a2 = new SecuredAsset(a1);
        System.out.println(a2.code + " " + a2.riskScore + " " + (a1 == a2));
    }
}
```

What does the following snippet print when comparing a copy factory method with a copy constructor?

```java
class ConfigProfile {
    int port;
    ConfigProfile(int p) { this.port = p; }
    ConfigProfile(ConfigProfile other) { this.port = other.port; }
    public static ConfigProfile copyOf(ConfigProfile source) {
        return new ConfigProfile(source);
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ConfigProfile original = new ConfigProfile(8080);
        ConfigProfile copy = ConfigProfile.copyOf(original);
        copy.port = 9090;
        System.out.println(original.port + " " + copy.port);
    }
}
```
